## Diligence Statement — Ledger AI

In creating this project, I collaborated with Claude (Anthropic) throughout the design, prompt engineering, and Python development process. Claude's role included: drafting the system prompt and iterating on it against my design decisions, generating the three mock SME datasets to a schema and set of constraints I specified, generating the 50-case evaluation suite structure, and writing the Python implementation (tool definitions, the conversation/tool-use loop, and the CLI) via Claude Code based on task prompts I authored.

I affirm that all AI-generated and co-created content underwent thorough review and evaluation. Every prompt was manually tested against real questions before being treated as final. The generated code was reviewed file by file against the original specification, which surfaced and led to fixes for three implementation issues before the app was first run: a tool name mismatch between the system prompt and the implemented code, an incorrect Australian BAS quarter mapping, and an error-handling gap in the CLI. A further issue — the agent misinterpreting relative time periods like "last month" against a static mock dataset — was found during live testing and corrected through two iterations, the first of which was itself only partially correct. All of this review, testing, and debugging work is documented with dates and reasoning in PROMPTS.md.

The final output reflects my own architectural decisions (the problem, the three personas, the system prompt's design principles, what "good" looks like in every test case, and which behaviours to keep or fix), not simply accepted AI output. While AI assistance was instrumental in producing the code, mock data, and first drafts of prompts, I maintain full responsibility for the content, its accuracy, and its presentation, and I have verified its behaviour directly rather than relying on AI-reported success.

This disclosure is made in the spirit of transparency and to accurately describe the role AI played in building Ledger AI.
